What will be the output of the following `ArrayList` manipulation code?

```java
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add("Java");
list.add("OOP");
list.add(1, "Spring");
list.remove(0);
System.out.println(list.get(0));
```

What is the output of the following code using a `HashSet`?

```java
Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
set.add(10);
set.add(20);
set.add(10);
set.add(30);
System.out.println(set.size());
```

Analyze the following `HashMap` operations. What value is printed to the console?

```java
Map<String, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put("A", 10);
map.put("B", 20);
map.put("A", 50);
int total = map.get("A") + map.getOrDefault("C", 5);
System.out.println(total);
```

What is printed when executing this `TreeSet` code demonstrating natural ordering?

```java
TreeSet<String> set = new TreeSet<>();
set.add("Banana");
set.add("Apple");
set.add("Cherry");
System.out.println(set.first() + " " + set.last());
```

What is the output of the following `PriorityQueue` code involving `poll()` and `peek()`?

```java
Queue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();
pq.add(40);
pq.add(10);
pq.add(30);
System.out.print(pq.poll() + " " + pq.peek());
```

What is the printed output when sorting a list using `Collections.reverseOrder()`?

```java
List<Integer> nums = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(5, 2, 8, 1));
Collections.sort(nums, Collections.reverseOrder());
System.out.print(nums.get(0) + " " + nums.get(1));
```

What is the final size of the list after using `Iterator.remove()` in the following snippet?

```java
List<String> items = new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList("A", "B", "C", "B"));
Iterator<String> it = items.iterator();
while (it.hasNext()) {
  if (it.next().equals("B")) {
    it.remove();
  }
}
System.out.println(items.size());
```

What is the printed output of this `ArrayDeque` acting as a LIFO stack?

```java
Deque<String> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();
stack.push("First");
stack.push("Second");
stack.push("Third");
System.out.print(stack.pop() + " " + stack.peek());
```

What is printed to the console after iterating over the keys of this map?

```java
Map<Integer, String> codes = new HashMap<>();
codes.put(1, "Red");
codes.put(2, "Green");
codes.put(3, "Blue");
int sum = 0;
for (int k : codes.keySet()) {
  sum += k;
}
System.out.println(sum);
```

